#: site:site.home.chain.heading
msgid "site.home.chain.heading"
msgstr "From an empty account to a code on the table"

#: site:site.home.chain.label
msgid "site.home.chain.label"
msgstr "The six steps, side by side"

#: site:site.home.chain.lead
msgid "site.home.chain.lead"
msgstr "Six steps, in this order. Every one of them works before you pay anything."

#: site:site.home.chain.step1.body
msgid "site.home.chain.step1.body"
msgstr "An email address, then the name, language, currency and time zone of your business."

#: site:site.home.chain.step1.title
msgid "site.home.chain.step1.title"
msgstr "Create an account and a business"

#: site:site.home.chain.step2.body
msgid "site.home.chain.step2.body"
msgstr "A branch has an address and its own clock. One restaurant is a business with one branch."

#: site:site.home.chain.step2.title
msgid "site.home.chain.step2.title"
msgstr "Add a branch"

#: site:site.home.chain.step3.body
msgid "site.home.chain.step3.body"
msgstr "Categories, dishes, prices, photos and declared allergens, in a draft guests cannot see."

#: site:site.home.chain.step3.title
msgid "site.home.chain.step3.title"
msgstr "Write the menu"

#: site:site.home.chain.step4.body
msgid "site.home.chain.step4.body"
msgstr "Publishing freezes a numbered snapshot. An earlier one can be restored."

#: site:site.home.chain.step4.title
msgid "site.home.chain.step4.title"
msgstr "Publish a version"

#: site:site.home.chain.step5.body
msgid "site.home.chain.step5.body"
msgstr "Export a card, a poster or a sheet to cut up, and repoint it later without reprinting."

#: site:site.home.chain.step5.title
msgid "site.home.chain.step5.title"
msgstr "Print a code for each table"

#: site:site.home.chain.step6.body
msgid "site.home.chain.step6.body"
msgstr "The code opens the menu in the browser already on the phone. No app, no account."

#: site:site.home.chain.step6.title
msgid "site.home.chain.step6.title"
msgstr "Guests scan"

#: site:site.home.contact.cta
msgid "site.home.contact.cta"
msgstr "Write to us"

#: site:site.home.contact.lead
msgid "site.home.contact.lead"
msgstr "Ask about pricing, a pilot, or anything that is in your way. We keep every message; you get a confirmation on screen."

#: site:site.home.faq.account.answer
msgid "site.home.faq.account.answer"
msgstr "Yes, create an account or log in to open the workspace app."

#: site:site.home.faq.account.question
msgid "site.home.faq.account.question"
msgstr "Do I need an account to try it?"

#: site:site.home.faq.cost.answer
msgid "site.home.faq.cost.answer"
msgstr "Prices come from our plan catalogue, so what you read there is what we charge."

#: site:site.home.faq.cost.question
msgid "site.home.faq.cost.question"
msgstr "What does it cost?"

#: site:site.home.faq.heading
msgid "site.home.faq.heading"
msgstr "FAQ"

#: site:site.home.faq.install.answer
msgid "site.home.faq.install.answer"
msgstr "No. The code opens a web page in the browser already on the phone."

#: site:site.home.faq.install.question
msgid "site.home.faq.install.question"
msgstr "Do guests install anything?"

#: site:site.home.faq.pos.answer
msgid "site.home.faq.pos.answer"
msgstr "No. It shows the menu and can carry an order to the kitchen. It does not take payment and does not know your takings."

#: site:site.home.faq.pos.question
msgid "site.home.faq.pos.question"
msgstr "Is Zabuno a point-of-sale system?"

#: site:site.home.faq.what.answer
msgid "site.home.faq.what.answer"
msgstr "A workspace app for managing a restaurant's menu and catalog and publishing it to a stable QR-linked page."

#: site:site.home.faq.what.question
msgid "site.home.faq.what.question"
msgstr "What is Zabuno?"

#: site:site.home.hero.actions.label
msgid "site.home.hero.actions.label"
msgstr "Account actions"

#: site:site.home.hero.heading
msgid "site.home.hero.heading"
msgstr "Run your restaurant's menu from one place"

#: site:site.home.hero.lead
msgid "site.home.hero.lead"
msgstr "Write a menu, publish it, print a code for each table. Guests read it in the browser already on their phone."

#: site:site.home.hero.note
msgid "site.home.hero.note"
msgstr "No plan needed to build a menu, publish it and print codes."

#: site:site.home.hero.openApp
msgid "site.home.hero.openApp"
msgstr "Open the app"

#: site:site.home.hero.register
msgid "site.home.hero.register"
msgstr "Create an account"

#: site:site.home.limits.dishNames.body
msgid "site.home.limits.dishNames.body"
msgstr "The interface around the menu speaks two languages; the dishes are written in yours and are not translated."

#: site:site.home.limits.dishNames.title
msgid "site.home.limits.dishNames.title"
msgstr "Dish names are written once"

#: site:site.home.limits.heading
msgid "site.home.limits.heading"
msgstr "What Zabuno is not"

#: site:site.home.limits.integrations.body
msgid "site.home.limits.integrations.body"
msgstr "Nothing connects to a till, an accounting package or a food marketplace. Your menu leaves and returns as a spreadsheet."

#: site:site.home.limits.integrations.title
msgid "site.home.limits.integrations.title"
msgstr "No third-party integrations"

#: site:site.home.limits.lead
msgid "site.home.limits.lead"
msgstr "Shorter than the parts list, and the part most software will not put on its home page."

#: site:site.home.limits.oneBrand.body
msgid "site.home.limits.oneBrand.body"
msgstr "An account holds one business with many branches, not several businesses."

#: site:site.home.limits.oneBrand.title
msgid "site.home.limits.oneBrand.title"
msgstr "One brand per account"

#: site:site.home.limits.reservations.body
msgid "site.home.limits.reservations.body"
msgstr "There is no table booking, no courier integration and no points card."

#: site:site.home.limits.reservations.title
msgid "site.home.limits.reservations.title"
msgstr "No reservations, delivery or loyalty"

#: site:site.home.limits.sectors.body
msgid "site.home.limits.sectors.body"
msgstr "No cafe version, bakery version or hotel version. One kind of business: places that serve food and drink."

#: site:site.home.limits.sectors.title
msgid "site.home.limits.sectors.title"
msgstr "No sector editions"

#: site:site.home.limits.store.body
msgid "site.home.limits.store.body"
msgstr "There is no iPhone or Android app for you or your guests; both sides are web pages."

#: site:site.home.limits.store.title
msgid "site.home.limits.store.title"
msgstr "No app in a store"

#: site:site.home.limits.till.body
msgid "site.home.limits.till.body"
msgstr "Guests do not pay through Zabuno, and nothing here prints a bill or reports your takings."

#: site:site.home.limits.till.title
msgid "site.home.limits.till.title"
msgstr "Not a till and not a payment system"

#: site:site.home.meta.description
msgid "site.home.meta.description"
msgstr "Zabuno gives your team a shared workspace to manage a restaurant's menu and catalog, publish it as a stable QR-linked page, and keep it updated as things change."

#: site:site.home.meta.title
msgid "site.home.meta.title"
msgstr "Restaurant menu & workspace"

#: site:site.home.parts.ai.body
msgid "site.home.parts.ai.body"
msgstr "A photo of a printed menu becomes a draft you approve, and dishes typed twice are found."

#: site:site.home.parts.ai.title
msgid "site.home.parts.ai.title"
msgstr "Zabuno AI"

#: site:site.home.parts.analytics.body
msgid "site.home.parts.analytics.body"
msgstr "Scans, menu opens, dish views, searches that found nothing and orders sent, counted by the server."

#: site:site.home.parts.analytics.title
msgid "site.home.parts.analytics.title"
msgstr "Analytics"

#: site:site.home.parts.branches.body
msgid "site.home.parts.branches.body"
msgstr "Any number of branches under one business, each with its own menus, prices, codes and hours."

#: site:site.home.parts.branches.title
msgid "site.home.parts.branches.title"
msgstr "Multiple branches"

#: site:site.home.parts.branding.body
msgid "site.home.parts.branding.body"
msgstr "A logo and two colours, frozen into each publication so a menu never changes under a guest."

#: site:site.home.parts.branding.title
msgid "site.home.parts.branding.title"
msgstr "Design and branding"

#: site:site.home.parts.heading
msgid "site.home.parts.heading"
msgstr "What is in the product"

#: site:site.home.parts.languages.body
msgid "site.home.parts.languages.body"
msgstr "The guest page follows the guest, dish names stay in your language, prices follow your currency."

#: site:site.home.parts.languages.title
msgid "site.home.parts.languages.title"
msgstr "Languages and currency"

#: site:site.home.parts.lead
msgid "site.home.parts.lead"
msgstr "Twelve parts of one account. Each has its own page where it is explained in full."

#: site:site.home.parts.media.body
msgid "site.home.parts.media.body"
msgstr "Photos are scanned, resized once and served small; the original is kept so copies can be remade."

#: site:site.home.parts.media.title
msgid "site.home.parts.media.title"
msgstr "Images and media"

#: site:site.home.parts.menuManagement.body
msgid "site.home.parts.menuManagement.body"
msgstr "Categories, dishes, prices and stock, edited in a draft and released as numbered versions."

#: site:site.home.parts.menuManagement.title
msgid "site.home.parts.menuManagement.title"
msgstr "Menu management"

#: site:site.home.parts.ordering.body
msgid "site.home.parts.ordering.body"
msgstr "Where you switch it on, guests build a basket and send it to a kitchen screen."

#: site:site.home.parts.ordering.title
msgid "site.home.parts.ordering.title"
msgstr "Ordering from the table"

#: site:site.home.parts.qrMenu.body
msgid "site.home.parts.qrMenu.body"
msgstr "Photo, description, price, allergens and sold-out state, at a permanent address that fits on a card."

#: site:site.home.parts.qrMenu.title
msgid "site.home.parts.qrMenu.title"
msgstr "QR menu"

#: site:site.home.parts.ratings.body
msgid "site.home.parts.ratings.body"
msgstr "A guest who scanned a code can rate a dish, and you can reply."

#: site:site.home.parts.ratings.title
msgid "site.home.parts.ratings.title"
msgstr "Ratings from the table"

#: site:site.home.parts.tables.body
msgid "site.home.parts.tables.body"
msgstr "A code per table, read back by a decoder before it becomes a file, printed as vector cards."

#: site:site.home.parts.tables.title
msgid "site.home.parts.tables.title"
msgstr "Tables and QR codes"

#: site:site.home.parts.team.body
msgid "site.home.parts.team.body"
msgstr "Editors, managers and a kitchen role that marks allergens and sold-out dishes and sees nothing else."

#: site:site.home.parts.team.title
msgid "site.home.parts.team.title"
msgstr "A team with roles"

#: site:site.investors.built.cta
msgid "site.investors.built.cta"
msgstr "Read the full inventory"

#: site:site.investors.built.heading
msgid "site.investors.built.heading"
msgstr "What is built"

#: site:site.investors.built.lead
msgid "site.investors.built.lead"
msgstr "The product has {parts} parts, and every one of them is read from the product’s own inventory rather than written for this page. If a part is renamed or dropped, this list changes with it."

#: site:site.investors.chain.heading
msgid "site.investors.chain.heading"
msgstr "What the product does, in order"

#: site:site.investors.chain.label
msgid "site.investors.chain.label"
msgstr "The product journey, step by step"

#: site:site.investors.chain.lead
msgid "site.investors.chain.lead"
msgstr "The base journey is the same for everybody and costs nothing: an account, a business, a branch, a menu, a published version, a printed code. Plans add capability on top of that chain; they never switch the chain off."

#: site:site.investors.commitment.cta
msgid "site.investors.commitment.cta"
msgstr "Read the service level terms"

#: site:site.investors.commitment.heading
msgid "site.investors.commitment.heading"
msgstr "What has been committed, and what has not"

#: site:site.investors.commitment.missingLabel
msgid "site.investors.commitment.missingLabel"
msgstr "Empty on purpose, in config/sla.php:"

#: site:site.investors.commitment.open
msgid "site.investors.commitment.open"
msgstr "No availability figure is committed. The service level terms exist and describe how availability would be measured, excluded, notified and compensated — but the values themselves are deliberately empty, because nothing in this deployment measures uptime yet and a promise nobody can check is not a promise."

#: site:site.investors.commitment.set
msgid "site.investors.commitment.set"
msgstr "An availability figure has been committed. The service level terms carry it, together with how it is measured and what happens when it is missed."

#: site:site.investors.contact.cta
msgid "site.investors.contact.cta"
msgstr "How to reach us"

#: site:site.investors.contact.heading
msgid "site.investors.contact.heading"
msgstr "Talking to us"

#: site:site.investors.contact.lead
msgid "site.investors.contact.lead"
msgstr "Questions about what is built, what is not, and how a claim is checked are answered from the same inventory these pages are drawn from."

#: site:site.investors.contactPage.commitment.absent
msgid "site.investors.contactPage.commitment.absent"
msgstr "No response time has been committed, so none is shown here. A fallback sentence such as “as soon as possible” would be a promise nobody made."

#: site:site.investors.contactPage.cta
msgid "site.investors.contactPage.cta"
msgstr "Open the contact form"

#: site:site.investors.contactPage.heading
msgid "site.investors.contactPage.heading"
msgstr "Talking to us"

#: site:site.investors.contactPage.identity.body
msgid "site.investors.contactPage.identity.body"
msgstr "The identity below is read from this deployment’s own configuration. Where a field says it has not been provided, it has not been provided; an empty field is shown rather than hidden."

#: site:site.investors.contactPage.identity.heading
msgid "site.investors.contactPage.identity.heading"
msgstr "Who you would be talking to"

#: site:site.investors.contactPage.lead
msgid "site.investors.contactPage.lead"
msgstr "There is one contact route on this site and investors use the same one. A separate investor inbox has not been set up, and pretending otherwise would send your message to an address nobody reads."

#: site:site.investors.contactPage.meta.description
msgid "site.investors.contactPage.meta.description"
msgstr "There is one contact route on this site and investors use the same one, together with the legal identity of the seller as this deployment has it configured."

#: site:site.investors.contactPage.meta.title
msgid "site.investors.contactPage.meta.title"
msgstr "Talking to us"

#: site:site.investors.contactPage.what.body
msgid "site.investors.contactPage.what.body"
msgstr "Say who you are, what you are looking at and what you want to see. Questions about a capability are answered from the inventory these pages are drawn from, so the answer you get is the same answer the product gives itself."

#: site:site.investors.contactPage.what.heading
msgid "site.investors.contactPage.what.heading"
msgstr "What to send"

#: site:site.investors.deck.evidenceLabel
msgid "site.investors.deck.evidenceLabel"
msgstr "Measured"

#: site:site.investors.deck.heading
msgid "site.investors.deck.heading"
msgstr "The short version"

#: site:site.investors.deck.lead
msgid "site.investors.deck.lead"
msgstr "The same facts as the rest of this section, in the order you would read them once. There is no file to download and no separate story: a deck that says something the product does not is a deck somebody has to correct later."

#: site:site.investors.deck.meta.description
msgid "site.investors.deck.meta.description"
msgstr "The same measured facts as the rest of this section, in the order you would read them once: what it is, what is built, what is not, what it costs, what is committed, where it runs, how it is checked and what nobody knows."

#: site:site.investors.deck.meta.title
msgid "site.investors.deck.meta.title"
msgstr "The short version"

#: site:site.investors.deckBuilt.body
msgid "site.investors.deckBuilt.body"
msgstr "Menu, publication, printable codes, photos, branding, languages, branches, reports, ordering from the table, a team and ratings live in one account, not as separate products."

#: site:site.investors.deckBuilt.evidence
msgid "site.investors.deckBuilt.evidence"
msgstr "{parts} parts, each read from the product inventory."

#: site:site.investors.deckBuilt.heading
msgid "site.investors.deckBuilt.heading"
msgstr "What is built"

#: site:site.investors.deckChecked.body
msgid "site.investors.deckChecked.body"
msgstr "Claims are tied to files and behaviour is tied to gates. A capability that disappears from the product cannot keep being sold on a page, because a red test says so before a reader does."

#: site:site.investors.deckChecked.evidence
msgid "site.investors.deckChecked.evidence"
msgstr "{sources} claims tied to a file, {gates} gate scripts present."

#: site:site.investors.deckChecked.heading
msgid "site.investors.deckChecked.heading"
msgstr "How it is checked"

#: site:site.investors.deckCommitment.body
msgid "site.investors.deckCommitment.body"
msgstr "The commercial commitments a buyer asks for — availability, incident notice, service credit — are written as terms but left without values, on purpose, until something measures them."

#: site:site.investors.deckCommitment.heading
msgid "site.investors.deckCommitment.heading"
msgstr "What has been committed"

#: site:site.investors.deckCta
msgid "site.investors.deckCta"
msgstr "Read the short version"

#: site:site.investors.deckNotBuilt.body
msgid "site.investors.deckNotBuilt.body"
msgstr "The product is not a point-of-sale system, does not take money from a guest, does not do reservations, has no third-party integrations and has no in-store app. Those are stated as plainly as the capabilities are."

#: site:site.investors.deckNotBuilt.evidence
msgid "site.investors.deckNotBuilt.evidence"
msgstr "{limits} stated limits, carried on the public home page as well as here."

#: site:site.investors.deckNotBuilt.heading
msgid "site.investors.deckNotBuilt.heading"
msgstr "What is not built"

#: site:site.investors.deckPrice.body
msgid "site.investors.deckPrice.body"
msgstr "The base journey costs nothing and plans add capability on top of it. Every price shown on this site is read from the plan catalogue, never typed into a page."

#: site:site.investors.deckPrice.evidence
msgid "site.investors.deckPrice.evidence"
msgstr "Prices are read from the plan catalogue and published at /pricing without an account."

#: site:site.investors.deckPrice.heading
msgid "site.investors.deckPrice.heading"
msgstr "What it costs"

#: site:site.investors.deckRuns.body
msgid "site.investors.deckRuns.body"
msgstr "One virtual server carries the application, the database and the uploaded files. Everything else that touches customer data is named, and named only while it is actually switched on."

#: site:site.investors.deckRuns.evidence
msgid "site.investors.deckRuns.evidence"
msgstr "{subprocessors} entries, read from configuration and the credential vault at render time."

#: site:site.investors.deckRuns.heading
msgid "site.investors.deckRuns.heading"
msgstr "Where it runs"

#: site:site.investors.deckUnknown.body
msgid "site.investors.deckUnknown.body"
msgstr "Demand, what a restaurant will pay, whether a restaurant keeps using it after the first month, and what it costs to serve one at scale. None of that is measured anywhere in this code, and this section does not pretend otherwise."

#: site:site.investors.deckUnknown.evidence
msgid "site.investors.deckUnknown.evidence"
msgstr "Not measured. The honest answer to an unmeasured question is that it is unmeasured."

#: site:site.investors.deckUnknown.heading
msgid "site.investors.deckUnknown.heading"
msgstr "What nobody knows yet"

#: site:site.investors.deckWhat.body
msgid "site.investors.deckWhat.body"
msgstr "One web product for places that serve food and drink: you write a menu, publish it, print a code for each table, and guests read the menu in the browser already on their phone. No app for the guest, no account for the guest."

#: site:site.investors.deckWhat.evidence
msgid "site.investors.deckWhat.evidence"
msgstr "The journey has {chain} steps, and each step names the controller that runs it."

#: site:site.investors.deckWhat.heading
msgid "site.investors.deckWhat.heading"
msgstr "What it is"

#: site:site.investors.heading
msgid "site.investors.heading"
msgstr "Investor relations"

#: site:site.investors.infrastructure.dataLabel
msgid "site.investors.infrastructure.dataLabel"
msgstr "Data it sees"

#: site:site.investors.infrastructure.heading
msgid "site.investors.infrastructure.heading"
msgstr "Where it runs, and who else sees the data"

#: site:site.investors.infrastructure.lead
msgid "site.investors.infrastructure.lead"
msgstr "This list of {subprocessors} entries is not written by hand. It is read from the hosting configuration, from the credential vault and from the measurement settings each time the page is drawn, so it cannot quietly go out of date."

#: site:site.investors.infrastructure.locationLabel
msgid "site.investors.infrastructure.locationLabel"
msgstr "Where it processes"

#: site:site.investors.infrastructure.roleLabel
msgid "site.investors.infrastructure.roleLabel"
msgstr "Role"

#: site:site.investors.infrastructure.unreadable
msgid "site.investors.infrastructure.unreadable"
msgstr "The credential vault could not be read while this page was drawn, so this list may be short. “We could not look” is not the same sentence as “there is nothing”."

#: site:site.investors.lead
msgid "site.investors.lead"
msgstr "Zabuno is a working product before it is a business. These pages say what has been built, what has not, and what nobody has measured yet."

#: site:site.investors.limits.heading
msgid "site.investors.limits.heading"
msgstr "What is not built"

#: site:site.investors.limits.lead
msgid "site.investors.limits.lead"
msgstr "There are {limits} things the product deliberately does not do. This is the section to read first: a capability someone assumed was there is discovered to be missing during service, when there is no time left to change anything."

#: site:site.investors.meta.description
msgid "site.investors.meta.description"
msgstr "What Zabuno is, which parts of it are built, which are deliberately not, what has been committed and what nobody has measured yet — with the file behind every claim."

#: site:site.investors.meta.title
msgid "site.investors.meta.title"
msgstr "Investor relations"

#: site:site.investors.product.heading
msgid "site.investors.product.heading"
msgstr "What has been built"

#: site:site.investors.product.lead
msgid "site.investors.product.lead"
msgstr "The product’s own inventory, part by part, with the file behind each part. Nothing on this page was written for an investor; it is the same list the product describes itself with."

#: site:site.investors.product.meta.description
msgid "site.investors.product.meta.description"
msgstr "The product inventory part by part, each part named together with the file in this deployment that produces it, and the seven things the product deliberately does not do."

#: site:site.investors.product.meta.title
msgid "site.investors.product.meta.title"
msgstr "What has been built"

#: site:site.investors.product.sourceLabel
msgid "site.investors.product.sourceLabel"
msgstr "Produced by"

#: site:site.investors.product.sourceMissing
msgid "site.investors.product.sourceMissing"
msgstr "The file behind this claim is not in this deployment, so treat the claim as unproven."

#: site:site.investors.product.sourceNone
msgid "site.investors.product.sourceNone"
msgstr "This entry names no file, because it describes something the product does not do — an absence has nothing to point at."

#: site:site.investors.rules.body
msgid "site.investors.rules.body"
msgstr "These pages carry no figure this repository cannot measure. How many places run the product, what it earns, how fast either moves, how large the market is and who else has praised it are counted nowhere in this code, so none of them is written here."

#: site:site.investors.rules.body2
msgid "site.investors.rules.body2"
msgstr "What is here instead is the work itself: the product’s own inventory, the file behind each claim, the commitments deliberately left empty, and the gates that check them. A test breaks the build if a number nobody measured is ever added to these pages."

#: site:site.investors.rules.heading
msgid "site.investors.rules.heading"
msgstr "What is not on these pages"

#: site:site.investors.verification.gates
msgid "site.investors.verification.gates"
msgstr "Gate scripts found in this deployment: {gates}. Each one is a check that runs against the real product rather than a description of it."

#: site:site.investors.verification.heading
msgid "site.investors.verification.heading"
msgstr "How a claim is checked"

#: site:site.investors.verification.lead
msgid "site.investors.verification.lead"
msgstr "{sources} of the claims on these pages name the file in this deployment that produces them, and each of those files is looked for while the page is drawn. A claim whose file has gone is shown as missing rather than quietly kept."

